          "source": "def-td-macro-versus-micro-entropy-claim",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The Boltzmann macrocell entropy of this specified coarse-graining is\n\n$$S_{\\mathrm B}(m):=k_{\\mathrm B}\\log N_m.$$\n\nFor a specified probability vector $p=(p_1,\\ldots,p_N)$, where $p_i\\ge0$ and $\\sum_{i=1}^N p_i=1$, define its Gibbs–Shannon entropy by\n\n$$S_{\\mathrm G}(p):=-k_{\\mathrm B}\\sum_{i=1}^N p_i\\log p_i,$$\n\nwith the summand $p_i\\log p_i$ defined to be $0$ when $p_i=0$. Both expressions have units $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, because their logarithms are dimensionless and $k_{\\mathrm B}$ has those units. The finite sum and logarithm have the meanings of [[def-finite-sum]] and [[def-natural-logarithm]].\n\nFor a density operator $\\rho$ in the declared finite-dimensional sector class of [[def-nrqm-many-body-framework",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2"
          ]
